      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-12933",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "First, we calculate $P(B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}+P(B)-\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ P(B) & =\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ P(B) & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region $A'\\cup B'.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/9856c9b0fdf3bf4b8f84417f6e625d823590f57dac4dcc8185994aef3f8c5e50.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP(A'\\cup B') = \\dfrac1{3} + \\dfrac{1}{6} + \\dfrac{1}{3} = \\dfrac56.\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/example-12933.json",
          "file_sha256": "8a3f8d8cd3d0b0b383414ae1789968188bdcce3dd76e7633375e13b6c51241ec"
        }
